# What each Russian letter arrives as: the code point a caller writes, and the
# byte of the module's alphabet the letter is read as.
#
# Russian has thirty-three letters and the alphabet Polish brought has room
# for no more than three new ones, so the letters take bytes the alphabet
# already has, each of which has a rule of its own in the dispatcher: the
# twenty-five Latin letters other than q, and Polish's eight, which come
# through q's link. Which byte a letter takes is only a name for it -- т is
# read as t and ш as w -- and lang/ruru/letters is written in the Russian
# letters themselves, through this file, so what each one says is decided
# there and nowhere else. ruru.statements says what kind of letter each byte
# is: ы, ё and ю are vowels there, and ь and ъ are signs.
#
# A capital arrives as the Latin capital where its letter took a Latin byte,
# which the module lowers as it lowers any capital, and as its own lowercase
# where its letter took one of Polish's, as Polish's own capitals do.
#
# Latin text in Russian is read by the same rules, as though it were the
# Cyrillic letter that took its byte.

0430 61   # а, as Latin a
0431 62   # б, as Latin b
0432 76   # в, as Latin v
0433 67   # г, as Latin g
0434 64   # д, as Latin d
0435 65   # е, as Latin e
0451 f2   # ё, as o with grave, a vowel the module takes as stressed, as ё is
0436 8b   # ж, as z with dot above
0437 7a   # з, as Latin z
0438 69   # и, as Latin i
0439 6a   # й, as Latin j
043a 6b   # к, as Latin k
043b 6c   # л, as Latin l
043c 6d   # м, as Latin m
043d 6e   # н, as Latin n
043e 6f   # о, as Latin o
043f 70   # п, as Latin p
0440 72   # р, as Latin r
0441 73   # с, as Latin s
0442 74   # т, as Latin t
0443 75   # у, as Latin u
0444 66   # ф, as Latin f
0445 68   # х, as Latin h
0446 63   # ц, as Latin c
0447 83   # ч, as c with acute
0448 77   # ш, as Latin w
0449 88   # щ, as s with acute
044a 78   # ъ, as Latin x
044b 79   # ы, as Latin y
044c 86   # ь, as l with stroke
044d 84   # э, as e with ogonek
044e f9   # ю, as u with grave: of the four accented u it is the one the module keeps to the letter rules rather than writing as u
044f 82   # я, as a with ogonek

0410 41   # А
0411 42   # Б
0412 56   # В
0413 47   # Г
0414 44   # Д
0415 45   # Е
0401 f2   # Ё, as its lowercase
0416 8b   # Ж, as its lowercase
0417 5a   # З
0418 49   # И
0419 4a   # Й
041a 4b   # К
041b 4c   # Л
041c 4d   # М
041d 4e   # Н
041e 4f   # О
041f 50   # П
0420 52   # Р
0421 53   # С
0422 54   # Т
0423 55   # У
0424 46   # Ф
0425 48   # Х
0426 43   # Ц
0427 83   # Ч, as its lowercase
0428 57   # Ш
0429 88   # Щ, as its lowercase
042a 58   # Ъ
042b 59   # Ы
042c 86   # Ь, as its lowercase
042d 84   # Э, as its lowercase
042e f9   # Ю, as its lowercase
042f 82   # Я, as its lowercase
